gestion, facial pressure or other nasal symptoms may require assessment to determine whether the sinuses are involved."}]]}],["$","div","3",{"className":"bg-white p-6 rounded-2xl border border-gray-100 hover:border-teal-200 hover:shadow-md transition-all","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-3","children":"Runny Nose"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed","children":"A persistent or recurrent runny nose may occur with allergic rhinitis, non-allergic rhinitis, infections or other nasal conditions."}]]}],["$","div","4",{"className":"bg-white p-6 rounded-2xl border border-gray-100 hover:border-teal-200 hover:shadow-md transition-all","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-3","children":"Sneezing and Nasal Allergy"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed","children":"Frequent sneezing, nasal itching and watery discharge are common symptoms of allergic rhinitis and may interfere with daily activities and sleep."}]]}],["$","div","5",{"className":"bg-white p-6 rounded-2xl border border-gray-100 hover:border-teal-200 hover:shadow-md transition-all","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-3","children":"Post-Nasal Drip"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed","children":"Mucus draining from the back of the nose into the throat may cause throat irritation, frequent throat clearing or coughing."}]]}],["$","div","6",{"className":"bg-white p-6 rounded-2xl border border-gray-100 hover:border-teal-200 hover:shadow-md transition-all","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-3","children":"Reduced or Loss of Smell"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-gray-600 text-sm leading-relaxed","children":"A reduced sense of smell may occur with nasal inflammation, sinus disease, nasal polyps, infections or other conditions affecting the nose."}]]}],"$L1c","$L1d",