d:["$","$L2c",null,{"faqItems":[{"q":"What is the difference between a cold and sinusitis?","a":"A cold typically resolves within 7 to 10 days. Sinusitis is inflammation of the sinus lining - usually following a cold - that persists beyond 10 days, or keeps recurring. If nasal symptoms with facial pain and discoloured discharge persist beyond two weeks, sinusitis is more likely than a prolonged cold and should be assessed by a specialist."},{"q":"Is sinus surgery painful?","a":"Modern FESS performed under general anaesthesia involves no external incisions and is not painful during the procedure. Post-operatively, patients experience nasal congestion, mild discomfort, and some crusting for one to two weeks. The majority of patients return to desk work within a week. Dr. kushwah uses a no-nasal-packing technique wherever possible, which considerably reduces post-operative discomfort."},{"q":"Can a deviated septum be fixed without surgery?","a":"A structurally deviated septum cannot be corrected by medications or nasal sprays - these can reduce the inflammation around it but not straighten the cartilage or bone. Septoplasty is the only way to permanently correct a deviated septum. It is a straightforward, low-risk procedure with a very high patient satisfaction rate."},{"q":"How many times do nasal polyps come back after surgery?","a":"Recurrence rates depend on the underlying cause. In patients with allergy-driven polyp disease - particularly those with asthma and aspirin sensitivity - recurrence without long-term maintenance treatment (nasal steroid sprays, saline rinses) can occur within one to five years. In well-managed patients who adhere to post-operative treatment, recurrence can be significantly delayed or prevented. Newer biologic medications (injections targeting the allergic pathway) can dramatically reduce recurrence in difficult cases."},{"q":"What causes loss of smell, and can it be treated?","a":"Loss of smell most commonly results from nasal polyps, chronic sinusitis, post-viral damage (including post-COVID), or head trauma. When caused by nasal obstruction or polyps, surgical treatment often restores smell significantly. Post-viral anosmia can improve with olfactory training - a structured daily smell rehabilitation programme. Early treatment gives better recovery prospects."},{"q":"Can children have FESS?","a":"Yes, FESS can be performed in children, though it is reserved for cases of chronic sinusitis or nasal polyps that have not responded to medical treatment. Adenoidectomy is often performed alongside or before FESS in children, as enlarged adenoids are frequently a contributing cause of paediatric sinusitis."},{"q":"What is the best treatment for allergic rhinitis in Delhi?","a":"Given Delhi's high dust and pollution burden, allergen avoidance alone is rarely sufficient. A combination of daily intranasal corticosteroid spray, antihistamines during peak seasons, and allergen-specific immunotherapy (desensitisation treatment) is the most effective long-term approach. Allergy skin prick testing is available at the clinic to identify specific triggers."},{"q":"How do I book a nose and sinus consultation in Delhi?","a":"Call or WhatsApp Dr. kushwah's clinic directly at +91-9311449825, or email drdhirendrasinghent@gmail.com. Appointments are available at both clinic locations - CR Park and Arjun Nagar, Safdarjung Enclave."}]}]
e:["$","section",null,{"className":"py-16 px-4","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"max-w-5xl mx-auto bg-teal-600 rounded-[40px] p-8 md:p-16 text-center shadow-2xl relative overflow-hidden","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"relative z-10 flex flex-col items-center gap-6","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-white leading-tight","children":"Book a Nose & Sinus Consultation in Delhi"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-teal-100 text-lg leading-relaxed max-w-3xl","children":"If you have persistent nasal blockage, sinus pressure, recurrent sinus symptoms, nasal allergy, nasal polyps, post-nasal drip, reduced sense of smell or difficulty breathing through your nose, an ENT consultation can help identify the underlying cause and determine an appropriate treatment plan."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"w-full max-w-2xl bg-white/10 backdrop-blur-sm rounded-2xl p-6 text-white text-left","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-xl font-bold mb-4 text-center","children":"Consultation & Contact Information"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-3 text-teal-50","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Call / WhatsApp:"}]," ",["$","a",null,{"href":"tel:+919311449825","className":"hover:text-white underline underline-offset-2","children":"+91-9311449825"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Email:"}]," ",["$","a",null,{"href":"mailto:drdhirendrasinghent@gmail.com","className":"hover:text-white underline underline-offset-2 break-all","children":"drdhirendrasinghent@gmail.com"}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"border-t border-white/20 my-5"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-4 text-sm md:text-base","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h4",null,{"className":"font-bold text-white mb-1","children":"CR Park Clinic"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-teal-100 leading-relaxed","children":["J-1981, Near Market No. 1,",["$","br",null,{}],"Below ICICI Bank, Bipin Chandra Pal Marg,",["$","br",null,{}],"CR Park, New Delhi – 110019"]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h4",null,{"className":"font-bold text-white mb-1","children":"Arjun Nagar Clinic – Safdarjung Enclave"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-teal-100 leading-relaxed","children":["19-C, Arjun Nagar,",["$","br",null,{}],"Safdarjung Enclave, New Delhi – 110029"]}]]}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 mt-2 w-full sm:w-auto","children":[["$","a",null,{"href":"tel:+919311449825","className":"bg-white text-teal-700 px-8 md:px-10 py-4 rounded-full font-bold shadow-xl hover:bg-gray-100 transition-all inline-flex items-center justify-center","children":"Call for Appointment"}],["$","a",null,{"href":"https://wa.me/919311449825","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer","className":"bg-teal-900/40 border border-teal-300/40 text-white px-8 md:px-10 py-4 rounded-full font-bold hover:bg-teal-900/60 transition-all inline-flex items-center justify-center","children":"WhatsApp Us"}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-teal-100 text-sm max-w-2xl","children":"Consultation is available by appointment. The appropriate treatment depends on the patient's symptoms, examination findings and underlying diagnosis."}]]}]}]}]
